# 9. Cross-Register Note

This manual documents the same feature twice. Identify one thing your
assigned feature\'s two sections handle differently --- something one
section states and the other omits, or something the two describe in
ways that do not match.

**What differs:**

Part 1 of Dataman states purpose through story/theme while Part 2 states
it as specific educational claims

**Part I says (quote):**

\"you\'ll be sharpening your math skills\"

**Part II says (quote), or is silent:**

helps teach the important basic concept of number betweenness\... and
number logic. The strategy\... will help build skills in estimation and
averaging.\"

**Why this matters to an analyst:**

Part 1 paints the story in a vague light using story and theme and
convey its points but doesn't give exact objective information that part
2 does. Analyst writing learning objective would need Part 2 since part
1 doesn't always provide specific context, leaving more assumptions than
actual observations

